.TH _CYAML_GET 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
_cyaml_get \- path-navigation back-end (prefer cyaml_get macro)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cyaml.h>

cyaml _cyaml_get(cyaml root, const char *path);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Navigate from root through a dot-separated path and return the node at
the destination.  Path components beginning with '#' followed by
decimal digits index into a CYAML_LIST by position; all other
components are treated as literal dictionary keys.

Escape sequences in path components:
  \e.   -> literal '.' in the key (not a path separator)
  \e\e   -> literal '\e' in the key
A '\e' before any other character is left unchanged.

The cyaml_get() macro is the preferred public interface.  Call
_cyaml_get() directly only when the macro wrapper is inconvenient.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Non-owning node reference, or NULL if any component is missing or the
node type at that step is incompatible with the operation.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_get (macro) (3),
.BR _cyaml_set_typed (3)
